WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.036 --> 00:00:01.266
- Good morning, Believe Nation.

00:00:01.266 --> 00:00:04.360
My name is Evan Carmichael,
my one word is believe

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:06.885
and I believe that
entrepreneurs are going to solve

00:00:06.885 --> 00:00:09.249
all of the world's major problems.

00:00:09.249 --> 00:00:10.606
So to help you on your journey,

00:00:10.606 --> 00:00:14.396
today we're going to learn
how to build self-discipline.

00:00:14.396 --> 00:00:15.989
Over to you, Terry Crews.

00:00:15.989 --> 00:00:18.533
(rooster crowing)

00:00:18.533 --> 00:00:21.015
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:21.015 --> 00:00:23.804
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:23.804 --> 00:00:28.117
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:28.117 --> 00:00:29.966
- The thing about self-discipline is that

00:00:29.966 --> 00:00:34.132
it is necessary for everything
you do in your life.

00:00:34.132 --> 00:00:36.751
You have to be self-disciplined.

00:00:36.751 --> 00:00:40.110
If discipline comes from somewhere else,

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:42.478
it's very very hard to remain consistent

00:00:42.478 --> 00:00:44.218
because you tend to resist.

00:00:44.218 --> 00:00:46.310
That's why because, I see trainers

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:48.430
and they're in the gym with people

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:52.468
and the guy or girl
that they're working out

00:00:52.468 --> 00:00:54.178
hates their workout.

00:00:54.178 --> 00:00:56.746
Hates it because the discipline

00:00:56.746 --> 00:00:58.281
is coming from somewhere else.

00:00:58.281 --> 00:01:00.081
It's something that you dread.

00:01:00.081 --> 00:01:03.302
Every time you go in, you
don't really want to do it.

00:01:03.302 --> 00:01:05.993
It's like, "Oh no, my trainer is here.

00:01:05.993 --> 00:01:09.334
"He's about to beat me up
and make me feel crazy."

00:01:09.334 --> 00:01:12.701
Well, the truth is every trainer

00:01:12.701 --> 00:01:15.635
should work his way out of your life.

00:01:15.635 --> 00:01:17.565
Anybody who's working you out,

00:01:17.565 --> 00:01:20.000
your teachers, your trainers your people,

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:24.111
they have to train you
to get out of your life

00:01:24.111 --> 00:01:27.600
so you can go ahead, do your own workout.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:31.310
Do your own thing,
practice self-discipline.

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:33.469
- Successful people have self-discipline

00:01:33.469 --> 00:01:34.883
but you have to make sure you're focusing

00:01:34.883 --> 00:01:36.244
on the right things.

00:01:36.244 --> 00:01:38.331
You can only force
yourself to do something

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:42.628
that you don't like for
so long until you quit.

00:01:42.628 --> 00:01:45.769
So I think too many people
have the wrong goals.

00:01:45.769 --> 00:01:47.256
Too many people don't
have the self-awareness

00:01:47.256 --> 00:01:49.125
to know what they really should be doing

00:01:49.125 --> 00:01:52.393
and have a strong enough why
to keep forcing them to do it.

00:01:52.393 --> 00:01:55.431
A lot of people who become
entrepreneurs start a business

00:01:55.431 --> 00:01:58.302
because they look at the
top 100 hottest companies

00:01:58.302 --> 00:02:00.987
to start this year and that's
what they want to go and do

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:02.657
because they think it's
going to make a lot of money.

00:02:02.657 --> 00:02:05.447
But if money is the only goal,
it's never going to work out.

00:02:05.447 --> 00:02:08.152
Money yes it's important but
there has to be something

00:02:08.152 --> 00:02:10.669
more important that you're striving for.

00:02:10.669 --> 00:02:13.096
If you look at the top
people in any field,

00:02:13.096 --> 00:02:15.598
they have deep passion for
their work that they're doing

00:02:15.598 --> 00:02:16.947
and because they love it so much

00:02:16.947 --> 00:02:19.287
it helps enforce the self-discipline.

00:02:19.287 --> 00:02:22.757
So the best way that I've
found to stick to a schedule,

00:02:22.757 --> 00:02:25.899
to make sure that I'm doing
the work that I want to do

00:02:25.899 --> 00:02:28.231
is one, make sure that
I have a goal in mind

00:02:28.231 --> 00:02:30.521
that I really feel passionate about.

00:02:30.521 --> 00:02:33.572
But then two, create habits,
and a morning routine

00:02:33.572 --> 00:02:37.052
and a schedule that support
me achieving that goal.

00:02:37.052 --> 00:02:38.564
So whatever goal you have,

00:02:38.564 --> 00:02:40.129
make sure that the work you're doing

00:02:40.129 --> 00:02:41.958
maps to you creating that goal.

00:02:41.958 --> 00:02:43.780
One of the hardest things that I find

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:46.027
is when I have a goal, and then I wake up

00:02:46.027 --> 00:02:47.855
and my schedule's thrown off.

00:02:47.855 --> 00:02:50.021
And this is going to
happen in life, right.

00:02:50.021 --> 00:02:52.328
That's why I try to create
a no-crisis business.

00:02:52.328 --> 00:02:55.019
But your schedule will at
some points be thrown off.

00:02:55.019 --> 00:02:57.008
You've got to drive somebody to work,

00:02:57.008 --> 00:02:58.652
or you've got to go to the hospital,

00:02:58.652 --> 00:03:01.233
or some crisis happens.

00:03:01.233 --> 00:03:04.048
I find it very hard to
get back on schedule.

00:03:04.048 --> 00:03:07.532
Just like if you are
trying to stick to a diet

00:03:07.532 --> 00:03:10.518
and you have that first chocolate bar.

00:03:10.518 --> 00:03:11.697
Chances are the rest of your day

00:03:11.697 --> 00:03:13.865
is going to get totally thrown off.

00:03:13.865 --> 00:03:17.536
So if you wake up and
you set a morning routine

00:03:17.536 --> 00:03:20.216
that sets you up for
achieving your success,

00:03:20.216 --> 00:03:21.777
you're more likely to follow through.

00:03:21.777 --> 00:03:24.288
As an example, if you want
to learn how to be fit,

00:03:24.288 --> 00:03:26.095
you want to learn how to
take care of yourself,

00:03:26.095 --> 00:03:27.500
you want to learn how to be motivated,

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:30.211
maybe waking up and watching
some Terry Crews every morning

00:03:30.211 --> 00:03:31.605
is a thing that you should be doing

00:03:31.605 --> 00:03:33.874
because maybe your
friends don't support you.

00:03:33.874 --> 00:03:35.175
Maybe your family doesn't support you

00:03:35.175 --> 00:03:36.742
but you've got Terry.

00:03:36.742 --> 00:03:38.234
You watch him, he's motivating.

00:03:38.234 --> 00:03:40.417
You want to go out and
do something bigger.

00:03:40.417 --> 00:03:42.649
For me, that's why I
created the top 10 series.

00:03:42.649 --> 00:03:44.712
That's why I created a lot
of the videos on my channel

00:03:44.712 --> 00:03:47.043
because I wanted to be surrounded

00:03:47.043 --> 00:03:50.410
with ultra-successful
people that I may never meet

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:51.829
and some people have passed on

00:03:51.829 --> 00:03:53.780
so there's never a chance to meet them.

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:55.608
But I feel like I'm hanging around them.

00:03:55.608 --> 00:03:59.117
And by watching their
videos in the morning,

00:03:59.117 --> 00:04:01.819
not at five o'clock in the
evening and hoping to get

00:04:01.819 --> 00:04:03.570
motivated for the rest of the night,

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:06.248
in the morning, to start my day off

00:04:06.248 --> 00:04:09.715
so that I want to go off
and do something bigger.

00:04:09.715 --> 00:04:12.894
So whatever that feeling
is, you have your goal

00:04:12.894 --> 00:04:15.752
and whatever helps you get
motivated and get that feeling

00:04:15.752 --> 00:04:17.964
that you can create on a consistent basis,

00:04:17.964 --> 00:04:20.091
watching a video, talking to somebody,

00:04:20.091 --> 00:04:22.253
reading a book, listening to a podcast,

00:04:22.253 --> 00:04:24.563
whatever it is, start your day with that

00:04:24.563 --> 00:04:26.787
so you have the right
environment around you

00:04:26.787 --> 00:04:28.995
to help you maintain
the discipline to go out

00:04:28.995 --> 00:04:30.368
and achieve your goals.

00:04:30.368 --> 00:04:33.558
So the question today is, I'm
curious what is the one thing

00:04:33.558 --> 00:04:37.456
that you're doing that really
helped you stay disciplined

00:04:37.456 --> 00:04:39.525
to achieving your goals?

00:04:39.525 --> 00:04:40.846
Leave it down the comments below,

00:04:40.846 --> 00:04:41.985
really curious to find out.

00:04:41.985 --> 00:04:43.015
I also want to give a quick shout-out

00:04:43.015 --> 00:04:45.725
to Aji from elyonconsultants.com.

00:04:45.725 --> 00:04:47.043
Thank you so much for picking up a copy

00:04:47.043 --> 00:04:48.860
of my book, "Your One Word."

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:50.369
Really really means a lot to me,

00:04:50.369 --> 00:04:52.195
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:04:52.195 --> 00:04:53.701
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:04:53.701 --> 00:04:56.896
I believe in you, I hope you
continue to believe in yourself

00:04:56.896 --> 00:04:59.221
and whatever your one word is.

00:04:59.221 --> 00:05:01.579
Much love, and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:05:01.579 --> 00:05:04.239
for another shot of entspresso.

00:05:04.239 --> 00:05:06.960
♫ I wake up every morning

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:10.420
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:05:10.420 --> 00:05:13.087
(typewriter typing)

00:05:13.087 --> 00:05:16.365
- So Tony, one of the critics
actually that I once met said,

00:05:16.365 --> 00:05:18.119
"Yeah, Tony's techniques, they were great

00:05:18.119 --> 00:05:20.079
"for about a year and a half,
and then they wore off."

00:05:20.079 --> 00:05:21.098
(Tony laughs)

00:05:21.098 --> 00:05:22.911
What do you say to that?

00:05:22.911 --> 00:05:24.194
- They're all simple,
if you don't work out,

00:05:24.194 --> 00:05:25.773
you don't get a muscle, right?

00:05:25.773 --> 00:05:26.606
So I always tell people,

00:05:26.606 --> 00:05:28.704
this is a daily practice, like priming.

00:05:28.704 --> 00:05:30.117
If you don't do that.

00:05:30.117 --> 00:05:32.537
If you get up and you just
have no discipline whatsoever,

00:05:32.537 --> 00:05:33.554
you get no value of anything.

00:05:33.554 --> 00:05:35.076
Diets don't work when you don't do them.

00:05:35.076 --> 00:05:36.577
Exercise doesn't work
when you don't do them.

00:05:36.577 --> 00:05:38.903
But most of people already
have some experiences

00:05:38.903 --> 00:05:41.586
that they want to shift, and
once you shift those things

00:05:41.586 --> 00:05:42.436
your whole life changes.

00:05:42.436 --> 00:05:43.946
But life is constant growth.

00:05:43.946 --> 00:05:46.297
My life isn't here because I
went to one seminar one time

00:05:46.297 --> 00:05:47.826
and now my life is fit for life.

00:05:47.826 --> 00:05:51.147
I work out, I train my
mind, I train my body.

00:05:51.147 --> 00:05:52.413
It becomes a lifestyle.

00:05:52.413 --> 00:05:54.584
It's not just like you're
depending upon somebody else.

00:05:54.584 --> 00:05:56.272
I'm not here to become somebody's guru.

00:05:56.272 --> 00:05:57.205
I'm not here to give them a gift.

00:05:57.205 --> 00:05:59.023
I'm here to open up their own gifts

00:05:59.023 --> 00:06:00.892
and that's really what my work has been.

00:06:00.892 --> 00:06:04.822
- I've never met a person
who is not successful

00:06:04.822 --> 00:06:05.989
that didn't have a great amount

00:06:05.989 --> 00:06:08.752
of self-discipline within their life.

00:06:08.752 --> 00:06:12.003
Self-discipline and being able to perform

00:06:12.003 --> 00:06:15.001
and being able to keep
your life on schedule

00:06:15.001 --> 00:06:17.510
and being able to keep
commitments and promises

00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:21.093
and meet deadlines is
essential to success.

00:06:22.065 --> 00:06:25.302
None of us can afford to have a life

00:06:25.302 --> 00:06:27.951
that is controlled by someone else

00:06:27.951 --> 00:06:32.291
or a life that is basically
controlled by our emotions.

00:06:32.291 --> 00:06:35.251
I learned many years ago that
there are two kinds of people.

00:06:35.251 --> 00:06:37.419
There's the type of person who says,

00:06:37.419 --> 00:06:40.579
"I'm going to wait until I
feel like it before I do it."

00:06:40.579 --> 00:06:41.665
And then there's a person who says,

00:06:41.665 --> 00:06:44.586
"I've got to do it so
that I feel like it."

00:06:44.586 --> 00:06:46.680
One will never get anything done

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:49.993
because they're still waiting
to feel the moment to move

00:06:49.993 --> 00:06:52.801
and the other person
says, "No, I need to move

00:06:52.801 --> 00:06:55.190
"and then I will begin
to feel the moment."

00:06:55.190 --> 00:06:58.738
Sonya, self-discipline
is essential in your life

00:06:58.738 --> 00:07:02.575
and in my life if we're
going to get things done.

00:07:02.575 --> 00:07:05.263
So I have a challenge for
every one of you this weekend.

00:07:05.263 --> 00:07:07.039
The challenge is simple.

00:07:07.039 --> 00:07:08.902
As you go through your weekend,

00:07:08.902 --> 00:07:10.443
and sometimes it's kind of,

00:07:10.443 --> 00:07:14.039
hopefully an easier time of your week,

00:07:14.039 --> 00:07:18.766
ask yourself, "Am I practicing
self-discipline in my life?"

00:07:18.766 --> 00:07:20.703
Am I doing the things that I should do

00:07:20.703 --> 00:07:22.364
because I need to do them or

00:07:22.364 --> 00:07:26.275
am I kind of waiting to feel the moment.

00:07:26.275 --> 00:07:30.131
Do like our friends
Nike say, "Just do it."

00:07:30.131 --> 00:07:32.781
- When I was in high school,

00:07:32.781 --> 00:07:36.281
I must have been maybe 16 or 17 years old.

00:07:37.706 --> 00:07:41.211
And I went rock climbing
in El Dorado Canyon,

00:07:41.211 --> 00:07:43.076
near where I grew up in Boulder.

00:07:43.076 --> 00:07:44.891
I'd been climbing for
about three or four years

00:07:44.891 --> 00:07:47.511
and I went to a climb called T2.

00:07:47.511 --> 00:07:51.224
Now, at the time T2 was a
relatively difficult climb

00:07:51.224 --> 00:07:53.079
and I went at it

00:07:53.079 --> 00:07:57.105
with a kind of an arrogant
lack of preparation.

00:07:57.105 --> 00:07:59.685
And I hadn't prepared for being able to do

00:07:59.685 --> 00:08:01.204
certain kinds of finger cracks.

00:08:01.204 --> 00:08:03.775
I figured, "I'll figure
it out when I get there."

00:08:03.775 --> 00:08:05.916
and I also didn't pause,

00:08:05.916 --> 00:08:08.377
and this I think is about
boldness and discipline.

00:08:08.377 --> 00:08:11.007
I didn't pause to really double smack,

00:08:11.007 --> 00:08:13.498
double check, all my systems.

00:08:13.498 --> 00:08:14.725
Okay.

00:08:14.725 --> 00:08:16.435
So I'm on the fourth pitch.

00:08:16.435 --> 00:08:19.435
I'm about 400 feet above the ground.

00:08:20.516 --> 00:08:24.045
I'm going across this
slanting crack system

00:08:24.045 --> 00:08:26.625
that I'd started to have trouble with

00:08:26.625 --> 00:08:28.663
and my forearm started to engorge

00:08:28.663 --> 00:08:31.110
with blood and lactic acid,
which means at some point,

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:35.884
even if you're on a big hold,
your hands are going to melt off.

00:08:35.884 --> 00:08:38.296
And I'm about to fall.

00:08:38.296 --> 00:08:41.126
I'm 400 feet above the ground.

00:08:41.126 --> 00:08:43.971
But it should be okay
because there's protection.

00:08:43.971 --> 00:08:44.882
I'm tied into the rope.

00:08:44.882 --> 00:08:47.693
I may take a fall but I'll get caught.

00:08:47.693 --> 00:08:51.505
For some reason, and to this
day I still don't know why,

00:08:51.505 --> 00:08:55.505
my brain triggered that
I should look at my knot

00:08:56.985 --> 00:08:59.395
and I looked down at my knot.

00:08:59.395 --> 00:09:01.395
My knot had come untied.

00:09:03.197 --> 00:09:06.766
I had made the mistake of
never really thinking about

00:09:06.766 --> 00:09:08.981
the best knots for certain
types of situations,

00:09:08.981 --> 00:09:10.856
and I'd tied in with what's a bowline.

00:09:10.856 --> 00:09:12.489
Now the advantage of a bowline

00:09:12.489 --> 00:09:15.465
is that it's easy to untie, right?

00:09:15.465 --> 00:09:19.573
The disadvantage of a bowline
is it's easy to untie.

00:09:19.573 --> 00:09:23.454
It had come untied as
I kept moving across,

00:09:23.454 --> 00:09:26.537
and it is just hanging in my harness.

00:09:27.503 --> 00:09:31.670
I'm seconds away from
falling, only now I will die.

00:09:32.795 --> 00:09:34.878
I will die if I fall off.

00:09:35.782 --> 00:09:37.782
My forearms are melting,

00:09:38.727 --> 00:09:40.546
and the knot had come untied,

00:09:40.546 --> 00:09:42.146
and so I called out to my partner.

00:09:42.146 --> 00:09:42.979
I said, "My knot had come untied."

00:09:42.979 --> 00:09:44.113
What is he going to do?
He can't do anything.

00:09:44.113 --> 00:09:46.671
He can just watch me fall to my death.

00:09:46.671 --> 00:09:50.957
And there was an old
fixed piton in the rock

00:09:50.957 --> 00:09:52.734
that was put there from the first descent,

00:09:52.734 --> 00:09:53.993
an old soft-iron piton.

00:09:53.993 --> 00:09:56.977
And I looked at it, and I
probably had 15, 20 seconds

00:09:56.977 --> 00:09:58.668
before my hands would unwrap, if that.

00:09:58.668 --> 00:09:59.501
Maybe 10.

00:10:00.674 --> 00:10:04.083
I took a runner, and I
clipped it into the piton.

00:10:04.083 --> 00:10:08.035
I clipped the piton into my,
that runner into my harness.

00:10:08.035 --> 00:10:10.535
And just went, "Please, hold."

00:10:11.532 --> 00:10:12.615
And I let go.

00:10:13.912 --> 00:10:14.912
And it held.

00:10:15.970 --> 00:10:17.932
I put in a backup.

00:10:17.932 --> 00:10:19.723
I grabbed the knot, retied
it, went to the ledge.

00:10:19.723 --> 00:10:21.180
I didn't convulse.

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:22.578
I was very calm at that moment.

00:10:22.578 --> 00:10:24.990
I got the ledge, I went
into convulsive shaking.

00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:26.941
I was sick to my stomach for days

00:10:26.941 --> 00:10:30.274
because of whatever happened chemically.

00:10:31.627 --> 00:10:34.900
What I learned from that is two things.

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:38.421
The first is that when you're
in an unforgiving world,

00:10:38.421 --> 00:10:39.771
gravity is unforgiving.

00:10:39.771 --> 00:10:41.796
It doesn't care.

00:10:41.796 --> 00:10:44.379
It never takes a day off, ever.

00:10:45.346 --> 00:10:48.026
And if you make one
mistake, it can kill you.

00:10:48.026 --> 00:10:49.405
If it's the wrong kind of mistake.

00:10:49.405 --> 00:10:50.488
What I learned is that sense of,

00:10:50.488 --> 00:10:51.679
yeah I want to do adventurous things.

00:10:51.679 --> 00:10:53.963
I want to climb rocks,
I want to be Yosemite,

00:10:53.963 --> 00:10:57.128
I want to do things that
get my adrenaline going.

00:10:57.128 --> 00:11:00.334
But I need the discipline
to always do all the right

00:11:00.334 --> 00:11:03.074
preparation, to always
think about the right knots,

00:11:03.074 --> 00:11:05.084
to always be crosschecking my system

00:11:05.084 --> 00:11:08.834
so that I can do those
bold things and stay alive

00:11:08.834 --> 00:11:10.466
in an unforgiving environment.

00:11:10.466 --> 00:11:12.269
And as you and I spoke
about earlier today.

00:11:12.269 --> 00:11:16.888
I think we're all heading into
an unforgiving environment

00:11:16.888 --> 00:11:20.175
where we're going to have to
be both bold and disciplined.

00:11:20.175 --> 00:11:22.300
The second thing I learned.

00:11:22.300 --> 00:11:26.041
What if that piton had not been there?

00:11:26.041 --> 00:11:28.953
We might not be here together.

00:11:28.953 --> 00:11:30.703
It was just by chance

00:11:32.594 --> 00:11:35.224
that that piton was right there.

00:11:35.224 --> 00:11:37.082
I want to you realize
when you rewind the tape

00:11:37.082 --> 00:11:40.804
of your own life, there
are these crucial moments

00:11:40.804 --> 00:11:44.221
where if the luck had gone the other way,

00:11:45.069 --> 00:11:47.560
you might have gotten killed.

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:50.432
So what you have to do
is always be putting

00:11:50.432 --> 00:11:52.989
those extra disciplines in place

00:11:52.989 --> 00:11:55.322
because I was lucky to live.

00:11:56.418 --> 00:11:58.148
And what I took from that is

00:11:58.148 --> 00:12:02.065
I never want to have to
be lucky to live again.

00:12:03.171 --> 00:12:05.941
I want to live because of my discipline,

00:12:05.941 --> 00:12:07.222
not because of my luck.

